This directory contains the following sub-directories:

 1. work           - contains the intermediate files produced by the
                     Synopsys 'analyze' command.
 2. db             - contains the synthesised blocks in Synopsys .db
                     format.
 3. log            - contains log files of the commands run during
                     synthesis for each block.
 4. scripts        - contains Synopsys scripts which are specific to
                     the EBI design.
 5. report         - contains reports written out by Synopsys.

Before start of synthesis scripts may require user modification.

1. The setup script, 'setup_scr.tcl' in the
   $GLOBAL/synopsys_shared/scr_common directory may need modifying for
     - the cell library location
     - location of the Synopsys read and write cache
     - Synopsys version specific variable settings

   Refer to comments in the 'setup_scr.tcl' script file for other
   parameters that might need to be modified.

2. The global script, 'global_scr.tcl' in the
   $GLOBAL/synopsys_shared/scr_common directory may need modifying for
     - max_transition and max_area settings

3. The timing parameters for the AMBA APB interface are defined by
   'apb_params_scr.tcl' and the constraints set in 'apb_slave_scr.tcl' in
   $GLOBAL/synopsys_shared/scr_common

4. The timing parameters for the non-AMBA signals are defined in the
   'Ebi_scr.tcl' file located in the ./scripts directory.
   These may require modification based on the target chip into which
   the EBI is being integrated.

5. The master compile scripts for the top level Ebi
   - 'Ebi_cmd.tcl'
   are present in the ./scripts directory.

6. The scan-insertion script - 'Ebi_scan_cmd.tcl' - is present in the
   ./scripts directory.

Synthesis Frequency
===================
The EBI has been synthesised at 190 MHz

Synthesis Invocation
====================
The specific synthesis run is controlled by the following variables:

TEST_METH
---------
The scan methodolgoy adopted during synthesis is defined by
the 'TEST_METH' variable.
It can take the following three values
   - noscan     - creates a netlist without scan structures
   - scanready  - creates a netlist with scan F/Fs but
                  without scan routing.
   - scaninsert - creates a fully routed scan netlist.

eg : setenv TEST_METH noscan
     setenv TEST_METH scanready
     setenv TEST_METH scaninsert

HDL_SOURCE
----------
The source code type is defined by the 'HDL_SOURCE' variable.
It can take the following two values
    - vhdl      [VHDL RTL]
    - verilog   [Verilog RTL]

eg : setenv HDL_SOURCE vhdl
     setenv HDL_SOURCE verilog

HDL_NETL
--------
The netlist type is defined by the 'HDL_NETL' variable.
It can take the following two values
    - vhdl      [VHDL netlist]
    - verilog   [Verilog netlist]

eg : setenv HDL_NETL vhdl
     setenv HDL_NETL verilog

dc_shell < scripts/Ebi_cmd.tcl >
    log/Ebi_$(TEST_METH)_$(HDL_SOURCE)_$(HDL_NETL)_run.log'

